<title>TAIWAN: Credit Lyonnais sets warrants on Acer.</title>
<headline>Credit Lyonnais sets warrants on Acer.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Lyonnais Securities said on Monday it had launched 10 million American-style call warrants on shares of Taiwan computer giant Acer Inc with an exercise price of T$52.5.</p>
<p>One warrant controls one share, Credit Lyonnais said.</p>
<p>The issue has a premium of 16.27 percent. The warrant life is nine months, meaning the warrants will expire on September 2, 1997, the securities house said in a statement.</p>
<p>On Monday, Acer's share price ended at T$53.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
